PATCH 137: SELECT PLAYER file-list dialog -- open + enumerate (*.FPL) + the shared display-list
container walkers.  Clicking SELECT PLAYER (menu row 74 -> screen-state 0xe) now opens the modal
list dialog and enumerates the seven player files (D, GAMESWIN, JO, JOE, KKR, PP, TRT) in the exact
DOSBox order (the engine's own bubble sort makes the order independent of the shim's find-first/next
order).  Reconstructions (all asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin):

  - e714 dispatch: state 0xe -> 0xe97c = e39f(); cb74(".FPL", si=0x451a title, di=DGROUP:0x77bc out).
  - cb74/cb7c (list-dialog front-end): the search pattern "*" at DGROUP:0xe844 is completed to "*.FPL"
    by `mov [0xe845],eax` -- a 32-bit store (asm 0xcb8e `66 a3`) that Ghidra truncated to a WORD (".F",
    0 matches).  Store the whole dword.
  - b756 (FILEMGR enumerate, asm 0x1b756): the get-DTA -> find-first -> copy-name -> find-next loop.
    Fixes three base-losses/dropped-returns: the get-DTA return ES:BX (DTA seg:off from the reg-file,
    not `unaff_ES`), the list-DEST pointer (ES=word[DGROUP:0x70]=STRSEG, dst=STRSEG:0x3776+cnt*0x10),
    and the name-SRC pointer (DS=DTA-seg, src=DTA:BX+0x1e).
  - b6dd (asm 0x1b6dd): the engine's own bubble-sort of the names -- base-lost (a83e/a840 were host
    pointers 0x3776/0x3786 -> non-terminating pass).  STRSEG-based, ascending.
  - cc33 (asm 0xcc8c..0xccb2): the modal list-dialog event loop.  Ghidra folded the two carry sources
    (3907 @0xcc8f, c40a/35a7 @0xcca4) to constants and scrambled the break, mis-exiting to the menu.
    Reconstructed faithfully with g_fist_cf threading + a cooperative INT-8 pump in the spin-wait.
  - 2006 (asm 0x2006) / 208a (asm 0x208a): the recursive child-list walkers that FALL INTO the 201a
    draw-walk / 209e paint-walk -- same base-loss class as 201a/209e (patch 056/057), reached for the
    first time by this dialog's container element (read the current element from DGROUP:0x3e08, recurse
    over [bp+di+1]+0x3af0 .. [bp+di+3]+0x3af0).
  - 1d84/1d8e (asm 0x1d84/0x1d8e): the dialog-position + mark-dirty walker.  Base-lost (whole walk was
    host-pointer-based) + WORD/int mis-scaling of every rect/link field; reconstructed with a shared
    recursive body (move each element rect by the target delta, mark dirty, recurse into containers).

The shim FILEMGR find-first/find-next (INT 21h AH=4E/4F) is implemented in re_out/fist_dos.c (not a
patch): it enumerates the real armoredfist/(FISTDATA) files matching the DS:DX 8.3 wildcard, sorted
ascending by 8.3 name -- reproducing DOSBox's DOS_Drive_Cache sorted enumeration (verified vs
ref/selplayer_native320.png), deterministic and identical native<->wasm.

FRONTIER (NOT yet bit-identical / NOT a verify.sh flow): the dialog OPENS + ENUMERATES correctly and
reaches the display-list PAINT phase, but the list-dialog RENDER chain is still base-lost/unthreaded
(the title-bar drawer ccca/b652 + the driver rect/line writers 119f/11ba/11db/1216/124b, then the
list-box text + selection highlight, the scrollbar, and the NEW/OK/CANCEL buttons).  Clicking SELECT
PLAYER therefore reaches this unreconstructed render and does not yet produce the DOSBox frame.  No
verify.sh flow clicks SELECT PLAYER, so mainmenu/about/settings/review + the default boot are
unaffected + deterministic (verified: 4/4 PASS, default rc=0).

